# Mongoose models

- One model per `<feature>.model.ts`. Only repositories import models.
- Define a TS interface for the document shape and pass it to `Schema<T>` / `model<T>`; derive the doc type with `HydratedDocument<T>` when needed.
- Always `{ timestamps: true }`. Mark fields `required`, `trim`, `enum` (from `@umc/shared` constants), `min`/`max` as appropriate.
- Declare indexes explicitly (`schema.index(...)`), including `unique` constraints.
- Sensitive fields use `select: false`.
- Read-only queries use `.lean()`; paginate with `skip`/`limit` + `countDocuments` and return `Paginated<T>`.
- Guard against re-compilation in watch/test mode.

```ts
export interface Project {
  name: string;
  code: string;
  status: ProjectStatus;
}

const projectSchema = new Schema<Project>(
  {
    name: { type: String, required: true, trim: true },
    code: { type: String, required: true, trim: true, uppercase: true },
    status: { type: String, enum: Object.values(PROJECT_STATUS), default: PROJECT_STATUS.ACTIVE },
  },
  { timestamps: true },
);

projectSchema.index({ code: 1 }, { unique: true });

export const ProjectModel: Model<Project> =
  (models.Project as Model<Project> | undefined) ?? model<Project>('Project', projectSchema);
```
